# The exceptions to the engine's rule against the console's terms (tools/engine_terms.zig, DESIGN.md
# P1, PLAN item 03): the legitimate cases only, such as a colour constant, or a chip's register in
# the sound's chip models. One entry a line:
#
#   PATH TERM -- WHY
#
# PATH is a file under src/shared, or a directory ending in `/`. TERM is the text as the source
# writes it (`0xFFFF`, `vblank_count`), or a class of terms: hex, vblank, register, vdp, vram, cram,
# vsram, cpu. WHY says why the term is not the console's place or name. An entry that allows
# nothing is an error.
src/shared/audio/chips/ hex -- the sound chips' models (YM2612, PSG, DAC, model 1): the chips' registers, tables and masks are the hardware's (DESIGN.md 10.6 A3)
src/shared/audio/chips/ cpu -- the chip models name the processors that write to the chips, as the hardware's documentation does (A3)
src/shared/audio/chips/ vdp -- the PSG sits in the console's video chip; its model says so (A3)
src/shared/audio/chips/ vblank -- the synthesiser counts chip cycles per display tick, the hardware's clock ratio (A3)
src/shared/audio/clock.zig cpu -- the sound's timing model: the drum hits held while a sample plays depend on the two processors' cycles, a named quirk (DESIGN.md 10.6 A4)
src/shared/audio/output.zig cpu -- the output stage times the samples in the processors' cycles, as the timing model gives them (A4)
src/shared/audio/output.zig vblank -- the output stage counts chip cycles per display tick (A4)
